open writes a hint-less file's hint before it cuts the torn tail, so a cut
that fails, or a crash between the two, leaves a hint over a file that keeps
the tail, and no later open cuts it. Reverts #476.
Guarded-by: "DB recovery: open fails when the cut of a torn tail cannot be synced*"

